@startuml recommendation-sequence-diagram

title Recommendation Sequence Diagram

skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant "GUI" as GUI
participant "Machine Learning Controller" as MLC
participant "Data Retrieval" as DR
participant "Dataset File" as DS
participant "Optimizer" as OPTI
participant "Data Manager" as DM
participant "Knowledge Base" as KB

User -> GUI : Selects a dataset and problem type
GUI -> MLC : Requests a recommendation for the dataset
MLC -> DR : Asks to load the dataset
DR -> DS : Reads the dataset file
DS --> DR : Returns the raw data
DR --> MLC : Returns the loaded dataset
MLC -> DR : Asks for the dataset's characteristics
note over DR : Extracts the meta-features\nthat describe the dataset
DR --> MLC : Returns the dataset characteristics

alt Problem type not provided
    MLC -> DR : Asks to detect the problem type
    DR --> MLC : Returns binary or multiclass
end

MLC -> DM : Asks to save the new characteristics
DM -> KB : Stores the characteristics
MLC -> OPTI : Requests the best matching pipelines
OPTI -> DM : Asks for the stored knowledge base
DM -> KB : Reads the stored records
KB --> DM : Returns the stored records
DM --> OPTI : Returns the knowledge base
note over OPTI : Normalises the characteristics and\nfinds the most similar datasets
OPTI --> MLC : Returns the ranked pipelines
MLC -> MLC : Formats the top recommendations
MLC --> GUI : Returns the recommendation text
GUI --> User : Shows the top recommended pipelines

@enduml
